WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.701
-Danielle Brooks,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.400
-I finally made it here!

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.434
-We're so happy
to have you here.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:09.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:12.701
I'm so excited that you're here
because I was reading up on you.

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:16.334
And there's an article where
they asked you, name five people

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.067
that you would ever have at
a dinner party, living or dead.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.501
-Mm-hmm.
-Do you remember what you said?

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:22.934
-I do remember a few.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:25.267
I remember my future husband,

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.868
which is now my husband,
so, hey.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.467
-Yeah.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.701
-Martin Luther King.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:33.367
-And I think I might have
mentioned you, Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.300
-Yeah, I'm on the list.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.634
-Which I'm a little salty.
-Why?

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:40.501
-Because you just had --
broke bread with John Legend,

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:41.667
ain't bring me nothing.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.133
[ Laughter ]
What's up with that?

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.734
-Next time you come on,
we'll get chicken and pancakes.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.000
-Okay, thank you.
-Alright, we'll do it.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.667
I want to say congratulations,
by the way.

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.267
You did -- You just --
You're married.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.601
You have a husband.
Your future husband you said --

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:53.868
what was it, six years ago
in this article?

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:55.400
-I know, I know.
-Here you are married.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.400
You have a baby.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.334
-I have a little one
who's a toddler.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:00:59.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:00.868
-How old is she?

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:03.334
-She's 2 1/2.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:04.968
-I know, it goes so fast,
don't it?

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:07.033
-Is it fun?
-She's amazing.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.133
She has so much personality.
It's kind of crazy.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.968
-She does, right?
-Yeah, she's crazy.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.534
-She has her own
Instagram account,

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:14.701
which every baby should have.

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.200
[ Laughter ]
-She does.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.901
-But she's very --
You did a very --

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:19.767
I mean, you're so cute with her.
I want to show this one

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.901
because this one --
it was #nopaparazzi.

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.767
-Yes.
-Right? And she's two.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:24.934
-Yes, let's see
what she was doing.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:27.367
-Take a look at this.
Watch this.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.400
-Oh, my baby girl.
-Look at this.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.033
-Who's that cool kid?

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.100
-No.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.100
-"No."
-Come on!

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.667
-"No." I know.
-The glasses.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.033
"No."
-"No."

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.834
And I did not tell her
to do that.

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.601
[ Laughter ]
That is her, all day.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.501
-That's the cutest thing ever.
-All day.

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:51.100
-You brought a photo of yourself
from --

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.501
I guess it was
a couple of years ago.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:54.734
-'Cause I've been wanting to
share this story with you.

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.400
-I love this.
-I think -- I don't know.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.834
When it happened to me --
-I love you saved it for me.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.534
-I low-key did, no lie.

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:02.434
When this thing happened to me,
I was like, "I want to tell

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:06.067
Jimmy Fallon this story one day"
because it was crazy.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.501
-Yeah. Explain this to me.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:10.601
Where were you and how did it
end up being where you were?

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:14.334
-Okay.
So, this is odd circle moment.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.801
Full-circle moment for me.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:18.801
-So, like, six years ago
I had to go to L.A.

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:21.300
And my homegirl, Gabourey
Sidibe, which I'm sure you know.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.334
All of us know Gabourey.
-Gabby.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:24.534
-What's up, girl?

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.133
She was like, "You can stay at
my place in L.A."

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.534
And I was like,
"Okay, thank you."

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:30.234
So, I get there. She's like,
"Look, I have a fancy dinner

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:33.467
that I have to go to, so I won't
be able to greet you."

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:34.934
So I was like, "Okay."

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.000
I got the keys,
get into her place.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.701
She has this pink robe for me
to put on.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:42.767
I take off my --
my bra to get comfortable.

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.534
You know, I was, you know,
living in there.

00:02:44.534 --> 00:02:46.300
She gave me some wine.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.734
So, I go to the back
and get settled.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.934
Drink the wine, come back --
try to come back,

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:53.767
and the door is locked.
And I'm like, "Oh, man,

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.968
she told me she got to go
to this fancy party.

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:58.434
I'm locked out of her house.
What am I gonna do?"

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:00.100
So, I call her.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.501
And she's like, "Okay, girl,
just come to the fancy party."

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:05.033
I'm like, "Oh, man.
I got this robe on.

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.834
I ain't got nothing to hold
the girls up.

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:07.901
What am I supposed to do?"

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.934
[ Laughter ]
And she's like, "Come."

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:12.100
-Nothing to hold the girls up.
-Nothing to hold the girls up!

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.434
Looking crazy.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:15.033
Right? Crazy.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.501
So, I go to get the keys.

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:19.567
And I'm telling you,
the Uber takes me to this place.

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:21.901
It ain't a house.
It ain't a mansion.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.167
It's an estate.
Do you know what I mean?

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:25.968
The service goes out.
Do you hear me?

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:28.200
That's how -- Yes.
The rich people live there.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.400
I get there, and she thinks
it's the funniest thing,

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.567
so she takes this picture of me
'cause she --

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:36.501
And so -- And I go into
the house and come to find out

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.634
there's this Victorian picture

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:41.834
of Samuel L. Jackson
and LaTanya Jackson.

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:44.033
I'm like, "I'm at
the Jacksons' house

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:46.901
and I got this pink robe on.
What the hell?"

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:49.033
-You're at Samuel L. Jackson's.
-Wearing that.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.334
-Here's the photo.

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:57.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.601 --> 00:04:01.234
-Crazy. Crazy.

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:03.100
But now I'm working with them.
-But look.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.567
Now you're working with them
on Broadway!

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:09.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what happens, folks!

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:11.234
Show up.

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:13.334
-Show up in the pink robe.

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:15.100
-Show up is the lesson
right there.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.501
Just show up
and you get it done.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:19.434
-Yes, and J.D. was there too.
Crazy.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:20.901
-Isn't that wild?
-Wild.

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:22.634
-That is just --
-Full-circle crazy.

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:25.400
-What's it like working with
the Jacksons?

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.968
-It's great, you know.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:29.133
It's like working with
your mama and daddy, though,

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:32.734
'cause them two together
is quite the fun time.

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:35.467
But it's fun.
We really have built a family.

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:37.567
The story is great.
I can't wait to be back

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:39.501
on Broadway September 19th.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:41.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
So, it's great.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.901
It's awesome.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.868
-You've had such a great run.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:46.300
I mean, Samuel L. Jackson.
-Yeah.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.901
-But also "The Color Purple."

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:51.300
-"Color Purple,"
which was awesome.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.901
Then I got to do
the movie with --

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:56.701
you know, being ushered in
by Oprah Winfrey herself.

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:59.901
It's been crazy. It's been good.
It's been good.

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.734
-But can we set up the --

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.667
I know it's August Wilson.
This is a revival.

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:06.901
Can we set it up?
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:10.634
It's about a brother and sister,
the sister who wants to keep

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:13.834
the family heirloom that has so
much rich history into it,

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.033
which is the piano.

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.701
And the brother who is like,
"Nah, sis.

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:19.267
I want to take this piano
and sell it."

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:22.467
-Sell it.
-Sell it and build
for the future.

00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:26.501
So, you watch them go at it
for about 2 1/2 hours or so.

00:05:26.501 --> 00:05:28.167
Come on, watch it.
-Yeah.

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:31.400
I want to say break a leg,
and I really want to say

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.400
thank you so much for
coming on the show, finally.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.400
The first of many.
Please come on.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.033
-Thank you.
-I will see you.

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:39.701
I'll be there. I'm not going to
tell you what night.

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.434
-Don't tell me what night.
-I'm not.

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.133
Do you like knowing?
-No.

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:44.701
-You don't like knowing
when anyone's in the audience?

00:05:44.701 --> 00:05:46.400
-No. But I still got to do
what I got to do.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.200
-I know. Do you see people
when you act

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.267
and you see people
in the audience?

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:50.534
-Once I see you, that's fine

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:52.234
but I don't want to
know you're there.

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:53.634
-I won't tell you.
-Yeah, don't tell me.

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:54.901
-I won't tell you
when I'm going.

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:56.267
I'll wear a disguise.
I'll grow my beard longer.

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:58.000
-Okay. Just put on a wig.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.467
-I'll put on a wig.
I got a lot of wigs, yeah.

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:01.634
-Like dreads.
-I'll put some dreads.

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:04.100
I'll put something on.
But I cannot wait to see it.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.501
Danielle Brooks, everybody.
Come on.

00:06:05.501 --> 00:06:07.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:08.634
That's how you do it
right there.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.334
August Wilson's
"The Piano Lesson"

00:06:10.334 --> 00:06:12.901
begins September 19th
on Broadway.

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:15.501
John Legend performs
after the break.

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.467
Stick around. How fun!

